*Exp 5- To perform brute force and dictionary attacks using hydra on an authorized test server to understand password vulnerabilities*

*Tools required : Computer / laptop, Windows OS, Kali Linux, Hydra, authorized test server, test username & password, Network connection*

*Theory:* A dictionary attack is a type of password attack in which a predefined list of commonly used passwords or words is used to find the correct password. It is effective against commonly used password. 
A brute force attack is a password guessing technique in which different combination of characters are systematically tried until the correct password is found. 
Hydra is a network login and auditing tool used to test the security of authentication services by performing controlled login attempts using supplied usernames and password lists. These attacks demonstrate how weak passwords can be vulnerable to automated password guessing techniques.

*Dictionary Attack*
In a dictionary attack a wordlist containing common password list to find the correct password. It is effective when users have weak or commonly used password

*Brute Force Attack*
In a brute force attack possible combinations of characters are tried systematically until the correct password is found. It can take a large number of attempts depending on the password length and complexity

